  "findings": [
    "The user-observed MLO stop remains valid but cannot be identified with the aggregate minimum at T+21.48..22.51 seconds.",
    "MLO nearest slow header at T+22.49 means reads occur during the recorded T+22.49..23.13 block, not at a precise point. On block-header times this starts only 0.02 seconds before the low-bin endpoint; fast counter read offsets and 0.01-second timestamp precision add uncertainty, so exact overlap is not established.",
    "The single6 near-zero bin at T+7.16..8.18 is wholly inside the T+5.62..10.63 no-collection gap.",
    "No same-time per-peer fastpath witness distinguishes global NPU worker stall from peer-specific scheduling/ACK behavior. Other-peer counter deltas span larger read windows and may be host/control traffic.",
    "All three cases have only 53 sequential PC reads per hart during the inferred traffic window; absence of a suspect PC is not continuous firmware liveness.",
    "PPE entries show registration, not per-flow progress. The observed token_count measures host SW in-flight tokens, not NPU firmware-token-pool occupancy.",
    "Lowest-bin per-CPU utilization stays below 6.80 percent in both the failed MLO and single6 slowdown trials, excluding sustained CPU saturation at this bin resolution, not sub-bin stalls.",
    "Status2 increments also appear in the non-stalling PS trace run. Continuous emitted log sequences do not recover rate-limited or ineligible events."
  ],
